specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:382:Answers one `list_sessions` request. It carries metadata only: each row has the conversation id, its creation and most-recent activity times as ISO-8601 strings, and its entry count; it never carries conversation entries or credentials ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:407:A store with no `listFor` answers an empty list. A failing `listFor` is logged under `ws` with the session and authenticated user ids, while the client receives `SERVER_ERROR` without store details ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L120), [validated by: reports a rejected conversation list without exposing the store failure to the socket](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L129)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:75:- A client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` and receives `{type: 'session_list', sessions}` for the socket's authenticated user, with `createdAt` and `updatedAt` serialised as ISO-8601 strings and any client-supplied `userId` ignored ([validated by: lists the session user's conversations with ISO dates](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L92), [validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:76:- A store without `listFor` answers `{type: 'session_list', sessions: []}`, and a throwing `listFor` logs an error on the `ws` category with the session and authenticated user ids and answers `{type: 'error', code: 'SERVER_ERROR'}` ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L120), [validated by: reports a rejected conversation list without exposing the store failure to the socket](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L129)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:77:- The validator accepts an optional non-negative integer `limit` (rejecting JavaScript's negative zero) and an optional `before` cursor whose `sessionId` is 1–128 characters and whose `updatedAt` parses as a valid timestamp, rejecting any other `list_sessions` payload with `INVALID_MESSAGE` without calling `listFor` ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L149), [validated by: accepts list_sessions paging values and rejects malformed ones](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L30)).

